  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191341/assets/4b0f9a0ac7d582b7e7b166596d55a1cca24f0176442dcb9c77731986b73d2969.png)\n\nWhat is the intersection of the intervals shown above, expressed as a number line?",
  "worked_solution": "The intersection of two intervals consists of the values that are in both intervals. So, it can be graphed by finding where the two intervals overlap:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191341/assets/0c273cc455592b9199c4c8447d77c077270b3c5cf05fcbfabe8baee07333acc1.png)\n\nTherefore, the number line that shows the common set of values is:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191341/assets/573a0ed4d14d765f1aa80929b32510eb4b28d101cf930df5c364dbab12999211.png)",
